{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "1 - Primary user flow: a click becomes a drawn relationship",
  "description": "Follow one scenario chip from the DOM click to the pixels: validation, the three trust classes, the bounded store, the in-place patch, and the readout that tells a reader which class they are looking at. Start the app first: cd render && npm install && npm run demo",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "render/demo/index.html",
      "line": 111,
      "pattern": "src=\"/demo/demo\\.js\"",
      "title": "The entry point is a plain HTML page",
      "description": "No framework, no router, no bundler. React, Sigma and Graphology arrive through the import map above; this module script is the whole entry. That is the claim the demo exists to prove, and the cost is that first load needs network."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/scripts/serve-demo.mjs",
      "line": 36,
      "pattern": "const relative =",
      "title": "Fifty lines of node:http instead of a static-server dependency",
      "description": "`/` serves the demo page; anything resolving outside the served root gets 403 before a single stat call. The two optional arguments exist so the SAME server can host `examples/compose`, which lives above this package and imports `dist/` from both layers."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/demo/demo.js",
      "line": 305,
      "pattern": "b\\.addEventListener\\(\"click\"",
      "title": "The primary user action",
      "description": "Every user action in this app enters here. Pressing a chip clears the previous scenario's timers, marks the chip active, swaps the caption, and calls run(). Ten chips, ten stories about the same trust grammar."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/demo/demo.js",
      "line": 21,
      "pattern": "const resetSession =",
      "title": "Each press starts from an empty session",
      "description": "resetSession cancels every pending timer and bumps a nonce that prefixes every eventId. Without the nonce, replaying a scenario would look like a duplicate to the deduplication memory in tour 3 and draw nothing."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/src/session.ts",
      "line": 253,
      "pattern": "^  observe\\(",
      "title": "Where input becomes trusted: the rule the product rests on",
      "description": "Two participants plus a measured count produce an `evidence` edge. Anything else (three participants, or a pair with no measurement) produces `traversal` telemetry only, because no measured pair count exists and no edge may claim one. A measured ZERO still produces evidence, with weight 0."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/src/session.ts",
      "line": 179,
      "pattern": "private upsertNode",
      "title": "The absence rule, in four lines",
      "description": "count === undefined means nobody measured this. count === 0 means somebody measured it and the answer was zero. A new measurement supersedes unknown; an observation carrying no measurement leaves the last measurement alone. Confusing these two is the failure this whole repository exists to prevent."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/src/session.ts",
      "line": 168,
      "pattern": "private trimNodes",
      "title": "Bounded, because the panel stays open all day",
      "description": "Nodes, edges and dedup receipts are all capped with FIFO eviction, and dropping a node drops its edges. This is working state, not the filing cabinet. stats() discloses the limits rather than hiding them, and the demo readout under the stage prints them."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/src/graph-model.ts",
      "line": 241,
      "pattern": "export const edgeKey",
      "title": "The edge key carries the TYPE, with endpoints sorted",
      "description": "Keying on (a, b) alone lets a traversal count silently overwrite a measured evidence weight, which was a real bug in the source repo. An unsorted key turns one relationship into two stacked edges carrying different numbers. Hence the JSON tuple [min, max, type]."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/src/graph-model.ts",
      "line": 264,
      "pattern": "const edgeDisplayAttrs",
      "title": "Only measured weights get the width channel",
      "description": "`size` is scaled from the weight ONLY for evidence edges; everything else gets a constant 1. And the scale is computed over evidence edges alone, so a 900-visit traversal edge cannot stretch the ruler that measured weights are read against."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/src/graph-model.ts",
      "line": 114,
      "pattern": "const EDGE_COLOR",
      "title": "Three inks, three luminances, and the collision that forced it",
      "description": "Read the comment above this map. Assertion and traversal were once 6.70 CIEDE2000 apart in dark, which is indistinguishable, and the docs promised a violet edge the renderer never drew. Hue alone is not allowed to be the separator either, so the three inks also hold three distinct luminances, which required WIDENING the dark ramp to make room."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/src/NodeGraph.tsx",
      "line": 171,
      "pattern": "patch = patchGraph\\(",
      "title": "Growth is patched, never rebuilt",
      "description": "patchGraph diffs the props into the live Graphology graph in place. Rebuilding would tear down the Sigma instance (five canvases and the layout) and replay the whole lifecycle per update, which reads as flicker. It returns WHICH elements were born, so the overlay can flare exactly those."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/src/NodeGraph.tsx",
      "line": 186,
      "pattern": "liveUntil\\.current = now \\+ 3200",
      "title": "Motion is bounded by data",
      "description": "An ingestion opens a 3.2s live window. The rAF loop in the cinematic overlay effect exits when it closes, so the steady state is a still canvas costing zero frames. Animation means 'the system did this just now', never 'the system is thinking', and never a magnitude."
    },
    {
      "file": "render/src/NodeGraph.tsx",
      "line": 958,
      "pattern": "data-testid=\"count-readout\"",
      "title": "The readout that closes the loop",
      "description": "Click a node and this is what a reader gets: the count, spelled 'unknown - not measured' when absent, and `visits` labelled in words as interaction frequency, not evidence strength. The receipt chips below carry source, release and a literal URL that replays the claim."
    }
  ]
}
